  <div data-dc-tpl="306" style="max-width: 1180px; margin: 0px auto; padding: 0px clamp(18px, 4.6vw, 48px); display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(290px, 1fr)); gap: clamp(24px, 5vw, 72px); align-items: start;">
    <blockquote data-dc-tpl="307" style="margin: 0px; font-family: &quot;Archivo Black&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: clamp(24px, 3.4vw, 38px); line-height: 1.15; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgb(246, 239, 228); text-wrap: balance;"><span class="sc-interp">"The birria alone is worth the drive."</span><footer data-dc-tpl="308" style="font-family: Barlow, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgb(214, 188, 133); margin-top: 14px;"><span class="sc-interp">The kitchen</span></footer></blockquote>
    <div data-dc-tpl="309" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: rgba(234, 226, 214, 0.85); text-wrap: pretty;">
      <p data-dc-tpl="310" style="margin: 0px;"><span class="sc-interp">Birria is Jalisco's slow-cooked answer to a cold morning: chiles toasted and blended, beef submerged overnight, then braised until the broth turns deep red and the meat shreds by itself.</span></p>
      <p data-dc-tpl="311" style="margin: 0px;"><span class="sc-interp">We do it the long way, every day, and never in a pressure cooker. The tortillas are dipped in the fat cap, griddled with oaxaca cheese, and folded around the meat. Dunk. Repeat.</span></p>
    </div>
  </div></section><section data-dc-tpl="312" data-screen-label="Ways to order it" style="background: linear-gradient(rgba(14, 14, 13, 0.78), rgba(10, 10, 9, 0.9)), url(/images/86475be0134bfc90.png) center center / cover no-repeat; border-top: 1px solid rgba(185, 156, 102, 0.2); padding: clamp(44px, 7vw, 88px) 0px;">
  <div data-dc-tpl="313" style="max-width: 1180px; margin: 0px auto; padding: 0px clamp(18px, 4.6vw, 48px);">
